Chapter: InductiveListTest
  cites Foreword chapter InductiveList

 A proof that inducts over a FOREWORD container.

 `codex/test/reverse-reverse` proves the founding flagship over a
 `MyList` it declares itself, and it had to: induction resolves the
 variable's type to a variant, the foreword's `List` is a builtin with
 no constructors to case on, and Stage 5 therefore accepted any
 induction over it as an unproven axiom (CDX4022). The same lemma chain
 is proved here over `Foreword chapter InductiveList`, which is a
 variant Stage 5 can walk.

 The instrument: this file must compile with NO CDX4022. A warning
 would mean the proofs were accepted rather than checked, which is the
 exact failure the entry describes -- so `inductive-list.diag` would be
 the wrong tool here, and the negative guard lives in
 `codex/test/errors/induction-list-false` where a false claim over this
 same type must be a hard error.

Section: Lemmas

  claim iappend-nil : for all (xs : IList Integer), ilist-append xs INil === xs
  proof iappend-nil =
   induction on xs
    is INil -> Refl
    is ICons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

  claim iappend-assoc : for all (as : IList Integer), for all (bs : IList Integer), for all (cs : IList Integer), ilist-append (ilist-append as bs) cs === ilist-append as (ilist-append bs cs)
  proof iappend-assoc =
   induction on as
    is INil -> Refl
    is ICons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

  claim ireverse-append : for all (xs : IList Integer), for all (ys : IList Integer), ilist-reverse (ilist-append xs ys) === ilist-append (ilist-reverse ys) (ilist-reverse xs)
  proof ireverse-append =
   induction on xs
    is INil -> sym (iappend-nil (ilist-reverse ys))
    is ICons (h) (t) (ih) -> trans (app-cong (cong ih)) (iappend-assoc (ilist-reverse ys) (ilist-reverse t) (ICons h INil))
   qed

Section: The Flagship, Over A Foreword Container

  claim ireverse-reverse : for all (xs : IList Integer), ilist-reverse (ilist-reverse xs) === xs
  proof ireverse-reverse =
   induction on xs
    is INil -> Refl
    is ICons (h) (t) (ih) -> trans (ireverse-append (ilist-reverse t) (ICons h INil)) (cong ih)
   qed

Section: Main

 The round trip is here so the chapter is exercised at runtime as well
 as proved at compile time. The proofs erase at emit, so without this
 the binary would contain nothing this file is about.

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let xs = ilist-from-list [1, 2, 3]
   in let back = ilist-to-list (ilist-reverse (ilist-reverse xs))
   in print-line-uni ("inductive-list: QED len=" & show (ilist-length xs) & " roundtrip=" & show (list-at back 0) & show (list-at back 1) & show (list-at back 2))
  end
